      "title": "Tennessee’s top prison official resigning after botched execution of Christa Pike",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/03/tennessee-christa-pike-frank-strada",
      "description": "<p>Frank Strada leaving position as state launches independent investigation into what went wrong</p><p>Tennessee’s top prison official is stepping down in the aftermath of the failed execution of death row prisoner <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/02/christa-pike-failed-execution-unconcious\">Christa Pike</a>, the state’s governor Bill Lee announced Saturday.</p><p>Frank Strada, the department of correction commissioner, will leave his position later in October as the state launches an independent investigation into what went wrong during Wednesday’s botched execution of Pike, according to Lee.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/03/tennessee-christa-pike-frank-strada\">Continue reading...</a>",
